+# Customer Care desk pack
+
+Three tools for the support desk. Run the commands from the Remit folder with `PYTHONPATH=src`
+(or after `pip install -e .`). All amounts are fictional.
+
+## Corridors
+
+Which routes we offer, what can be sent on each, how it is delivered and which fee schedule applies.
+
+```bash
+python -m remit corridors            # every corridor, ordered by code
+python -m remit corridors QAR-PKR    # one corridor
+```
+
+```text
+QAR-INR: 50.00 to 25000.00 QAR; delivery: bank_deposit (default), wallet; fees: STD-A
+```
+
+An unknown code prints `error [unknown_corridor]` and exits with 1.
+
+## Limits
+
+Where a customer stands against their daily and monthly sending limits (the Qatar day and month).
+
+```bash
+python -m remit limits --customer C001
+```
+
+```text
+C001  Aisha Rahman
+T2: today 500.00 of 10000.00 QAR used (9500.00 left); this month 500.00 of 40000.00 QAR used (39500.00 left)
+```
+
+An unknown customer prints `error [unknown_customer]` and exits with 1.
+
+## Delay message
+
+When a transfer is late, send the customer the `transfer_delayed` notification. Customer Care
+approved this wording; the Arabic version is in `src/remit/notify.py`.
+
+> Hi {name}, your transfer {transfer_id} to {recipient} is taking longer than expected. We are
+> working on it and will message you as soon as it arrives. We are sorry for the wait.
